## Demo 2: Send / Recv in Code

## Core rank-specific branches after MPI initialization

if (rank == 0) {
    int x = 42;
    MPI_Send(&x, 1, MPI_INT, 1, 0, MPI_COMM_WORLD);
} else if (rank == 1) {
    int x;
    MPI_Recv(&x, 1, MPI_INT, 0, 0, MPI_COMM_WORLD, MPI_STATUS_IGNORE);
}

## Argument Guide


<table border=1 style='margin: auto; word-wrap: break-word;'><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>buffer</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>Pointer to data</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>count</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>Number of elements</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>datatype</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>Data type of elements</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>destination / source</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>Rank of peer</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>tag</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>User-defined identifier</td></tr><tr><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>communicator</td><td style='text-align: center; word-wrap: break-word;'>Communication context</td></tr></table>

## Walkthrough

1. Rank O creates x

2. Send and receive descriptions correspond

3. Rank 1 obtains x = 42

## Message Matching

Must match before Rank 1 can receive:

✓ buffer

✓ count

✓ datatype

✓ destination / source

✓ tag

✓ communicator

Same message description, different endpoint roles.

